//This is the file which merges the pharmacy files in and keeps track of whether individuals are or or not filling the meds in their regimen on a day to day basis.

//First, we open the long form data file:
use "Data ExpandedCD4VLDemo $DateOfAnalysis.dta", clear


//Merge the CurrentRegimen file and drop individuals who never were dispensed medications
merge m:1 studyid using "Data CurrentRegimen $DateOfAnalysis.dta"
tab studyid if _merge==1
drop if _merge==1
drop _merge

Carry the regimen forward
Each regimen is placed on the day it started and filled down until the next one starts. new_regimen marks the start days. A regimen that started before 1 January 2008 is not on the grid, so those days have no regimen until the next start: exactly what the Stata did, since it only matched start dates that fell inside the window.


Click to show/hide R Code
# Each regimen is placed on its start date and carried forward until the next
# one starts. Days before the first regimen in the study window have none.
daily &lt;- daily |&gt;
  left_join(regimen_episodes, by = c("studyid", "date" = "regimen_start")) |&gt;
  mutate(new_regimen = !is.na(regimen_number)) |&gt;
  arrange(studyid, date) |&gt;
  group_by(studyid) |&gt;
  fill(regimen, regimen_number, bid_regimen, .direction = "down") |&gt;
  ungroup()





